1
00:00:00,006 --> 00:00:01,580
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,582 --> 00:00:03,011
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,785 --> 00:00:05,380
Stop changing the subject!

4
00:00:05,694 --> 00:00:07,778
- Did you see it or not?
- Na Ji Ni!

5
00:00:08,598 --> 00:00:09,866
If you really didn't see it,

6
00:00:10,173 --> 00:00:11,825
I'll show this to Yeong Ju.

7
00:00:11,919 --> 00:00:13,377
Fine. Show her.

8
00:00:13,491 --> 00:00:15,471
Go ahead! Show her!

9
00:00:25,964 --> 00:00:27,850
(Family Register)

10
00:00:58,505 --> 00:01:00,207
I'm sorry I doubted you.

11
00:01:01,972 --> 00:01:03,445
I should be the one apologizing.

12
00:01:03,878 --> 00:01:05,864
You've had such a hard life
because I'm your mom.

13
00:01:06,004 --> 00:01:07,004
Mom.

14
00:01:07,612 --> 00:01:11,135
You understand your dad,
so why are you so hard on me?

15
00:01:13,462 --> 00:01:16,106
Dad apologized to me.
He said he was sorry.

16
00:01:16,991 --> 00:01:19,006
He said he was sorry for making me
live with my head down.

17
00:01:19,752 --> 00:01:21,050
But you never did.

18
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:25,005
You told me to hold my head high
and live with confidence.

19
00:01:25,798 --> 00:01:27,175
I don't like that version of you, Mom.

20
00:01:27,432 --> 00:01:29,352
What do I have to hold my head high
and be confident about?

21
00:01:29,392 --> 00:01:32,003
If you bow your head,
they'll just walk all over you.

22
00:01:32,931 --> 00:01:35,404
I came here, got on my knees, and begged,

23
00:01:35,491 --> 00:01:36,924
but they just threw water on me.

24
00:01:37,118 --> 00:01:38,819
They won't even let me near the place.

25
00:01:39,158 --> 00:01:40,496
So why should I beg?

26
00:01:41,245 --> 00:01:44,251
They made sure you'd be Na Ji Ni forever,
no matter how much I begged.

27
00:01:46,632 --> 00:01:49,449
Okay. I'm sorry I doubted you.

28
00:01:50,445 --> 00:01:54,310
You judge me more harshly
than anyone else.

29
00:01:54,538 --> 00:01:55,776
You're no daughter of mine.

30
00:01:57,528 --> 00:01:59,118
I'm sorry, Mom.

31
00:02:00,358 --> 00:02:01,358
But...

32
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:03,898
I was shocked when I saw that photo too.

33
00:02:03,952 --> 00:02:06,326
I mean, how could you not have seen it
from that angle?

34
00:02:07,091 --> 00:02:10,852
That's why I came to you first
instead of telling anyone else.

35
00:02:10,898 --> 00:02:12,652
I wanted to ask you first.

36
00:02:13,571 --> 00:02:15,856
That's the same as accusing me.

37
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:18,451
I don't even know why I bother living.

38
00:02:18,625 --> 00:02:21,519
Even if I'd done it,
you should've been on my side.

39
00:02:21,672 --> 00:02:22,996
Why would I do that?

40
00:02:23,058 --> 00:02:25,705
I was trying to protect you and your dad!

41
00:02:27,971 --> 00:02:29,063
No.

42
00:02:29,094 --> 00:02:31,578
That's not true at all.
Don't look at me like that.

43
00:02:31,632 --> 00:02:32,913
I didn't see it.

44
00:02:33,529 --> 00:02:34,837
You little brat!

45
00:02:34,892 --> 00:02:36,688
You've never been on my side.

46
00:02:36,845 --> 00:02:38,731
From the moment I got pregnant with you,

47
00:02:38,903 --> 00:02:41,725
you've never understood
how hard my life has been.

48
00:02:42,465 --> 00:02:44,225
I just want us to be...

49
00:02:44,579 --> 00:02:46,998
like other mothers and daughters,
supporting each other.

50
00:02:46,999 --> 00:02:48,257
Don't lie to me.

51
00:02:48,843 --> 00:02:49,843
Go.

52
00:02:50,218 --> 00:02:53,398
Go be happy with your precious Yeong Ju.

53
00:02:53,685 --> 00:02:57,670
I'll just stay here
until I'm worn out and die.

54
00:02:57,785 --> 00:02:59,048
I have nothing left to lose.

55
00:03:22,631 --> 00:03:25,209
- I'm home.
- You're back?

56
00:03:25,805 --> 00:03:28,172
- Want some grapes?
- Yes, please.

57
00:03:35,032 --> 00:03:36,958
- Try some.
- Okay.

58
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,799
I gave Ji Hu the Polaroid.

59
00:03:42,104 --> 00:03:43,104
Okay.

60
00:03:50,198 --> 00:03:51,442
Well...

61
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:53,607
Here.

62
00:03:54,542 --> 00:03:55,653
What's this?

63
00:04:02,238 --> 00:04:03,238
Ji Ni.

64
00:04:03,365 --> 00:04:07,249
You mentioned the camera earlier,
so I searched my old things and found it.

65
00:04:08,231 --> 00:04:10,098
I wish I'd seen it sooner.

66
00:04:10,783 --> 00:04:13,765
I saw the photo and went straight to Mom,
hurting her in the process.

67
00:04:14,185 --> 00:04:17,342
I didn't think it was possible
to miss this while driving.

68
00:04:20,545 --> 00:04:21,820
Your mom said that back then...

69
00:04:22,464 --> 00:04:25,331
she was driving
and turned out of the alley right away.

70
00:04:26,125 --> 00:04:29,918
Your grandpa grilled your dad
like he was ready to hit him.

71
00:04:31,505 --> 00:04:34,895
He said a father had pretended not to see
his own child following him.

72
00:04:35,877 --> 00:04:37,305
He deserved to be scolded.

73
00:04:39,811 --> 00:04:43,438
She'd said several times
that she hadn't seen him.

74
00:04:45,652 --> 00:04:49,507
Like you said,
I wish we'd found this camera sooner.

75
00:04:50,561 --> 00:04:52,127
So this is the guy, then.

76
00:04:56,205 --> 00:04:57,205
Back then,

77
00:04:58,382 --> 00:05:01,105
Grandpa transferred the Seo Chon house
into my name.

78
00:05:02,011 --> 00:05:03,122
Actually,

79
00:05:04,037 --> 00:05:05,736
I'd agreed to give the papers
to your mom...

80
00:05:06,404 --> 00:05:08,498
and then leave.

81
00:05:12,911 --> 00:05:14,305
If it hadn't been for this incident,

82
00:05:15,454 --> 00:05:19,094
you could've become Cha Ji Ni,
and things might've been better.

83
00:05:23,385 --> 00:05:26,633
Even when you're angry,
watch how you speak to your mom.

84
00:05:26,845 --> 00:05:31,011
Just like your mom said,
she lived that way just to protect you.

85
00:05:34,734 --> 00:05:38,302
I showed your eldest son, too,
on my way here.

86
00:05:38,350 --> 00:05:39,847
He happened to walk in.

87
00:05:41,064 --> 00:05:44,379
Don't call him "my eldest son."
Call him "big brother."

88
00:05:44,975 --> 00:05:46,623
How could I do that?

89
00:05:48,858 --> 00:05:50,855
You're so stubborn.

90
00:05:55,191 --> 00:05:56,605
He was living in a shipping container.

91
00:05:56,818 --> 00:05:59,649
He only finished middle school,
so he got a Grade 4 military rating.

92
00:05:59,651 --> 00:06:01,225
And after years on the waiting list,
he was exempted.

93
00:06:01,705 --> 00:06:04,615
His dad is dead,
and his mom abandoned him and is missing.

94
00:06:05,263 --> 00:06:06,263
Missing?

95
00:06:06,625 --> 00:06:08,838
- So he lives alone?
- Yes.

96
00:06:09,078 --> 00:06:10,758
She borrowed money from someone like him?

97
00:06:11,532 --> 00:06:13,398
I found that rather strange too.

98
00:06:13,838 --> 00:06:16,756
He has absolutely no assets.

99
00:06:18,625 --> 00:06:20,590
So someone else is pulling the strings.

100
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:22,080
Most likely.

101
00:06:22,825 --> 00:06:27,066
I went into his place,
but it was gloomy and gave me the creeps.

102
00:06:27,432 --> 00:06:29,934
How did Se Ri
end up with a guy like that...

103
00:06:31,562 --> 00:06:33,933
- Keep a close eye on him.
- Yes, sir.

104
00:06:44,318 --> 00:06:46,203
Mother, it's Ji Hu.

105
00:06:47,478 --> 00:06:49,715
Did something happen
between you and Ji Ni?

106
00:06:50,832 --> 00:06:53,404
She won't say anything,
but that's how it feels.

107
00:06:54,558 --> 00:06:57,092
I thought you might be having a hard time,
so I wanted to check in.

108
00:06:58,431 --> 00:07:00,469
Even if you're upset,
please make sure to eat.

109
00:07:00,798 --> 00:07:02,702
Don't let what she said get to you.

110
00:07:03,072 --> 00:07:04,072
Have a good night.

111
00:07:06,344 --> 00:07:07,344
What a sweetheart!

112
00:07:10,102 --> 00:07:11,715
He's better than my own daughter.

113
00:07:31,422 --> 00:07:33,144
(Na Se Ri)

114
00:07:37,258 --> 00:07:38,905
I like it.

115
00:07:44,472 --> 00:07:45,472
What is it now?

116
00:07:48,285 --> 00:07:49,483
I don't even want to talk.

117
00:07:52,684 --> 00:07:55,378
- That looks good.
- Does it, though?

118
00:07:55,405 --> 00:07:58,878
Dragging someone else's son around
like that? Doesn't she have any shame?

119
00:07:59,952 --> 00:08:01,740
And now she's going after
her daughter's man too?

120
00:08:02,772 --> 00:08:05,066
Why do you have to be so vulgar?

121
00:08:05,282 --> 00:08:07,056
- Going after him?
- What else would you call it?

122
00:08:07,058 --> 00:08:09,685
A mother-in-law doting on her son-in-law.
What's wrong with that?

123
00:08:10,492 --> 00:08:12,721
You should be nicer to Ji Ni too.

124
00:08:13,212 --> 00:08:14,698
Stop favoring only Jung A.

125
00:08:14,765 --> 00:08:16,291
You're the one who's embarrassing.

126
00:08:16,292 --> 00:08:19,406
They act so differently.
How can I treat them the same?

127
00:08:20,052 --> 00:08:21,832
You saw it that day too.

128
00:08:21,858 --> 00:08:25,631
Jung A was all smiles, calling us
Mother and Father.

129
00:08:26,452 --> 00:08:30,683
Our daughter-in-law, Genie or whatever,
just sat there sulking in silence.

130
00:08:30,884 --> 00:08:33,318
Love is what you make of it.

131
00:08:33,319 --> 00:08:34,978
That's why I feel sorry for her.

132
00:08:35,218 --> 00:08:37,758
She never had the freedom
to express how she really felt.

133
00:08:38,071 --> 00:08:39,289
Please treat her better.

134
00:08:39,531 --> 00:08:41,091
You're the elder here. You're her mother.

135
00:08:42,185 --> 00:08:43,878
I have no intention of doing that.

136
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:16,618
- What is it?
- It's already 8 a.m.

137
00:09:17,011 --> 00:09:19,489
I know you're self-employed,
but you shouldn't be sleeping this late.

138
00:09:20,052 --> 00:09:21,901
I came to wake you up. Breakfast is ready.

139
00:09:22,502 --> 00:09:23,678
No need to jump.

140
00:09:34,125 --> 00:09:35,125
Where's Seung Hyun?

141
00:09:36,048 --> 00:09:37,948
He must've left early.

142
00:09:39,145 --> 00:09:41,456
I didn't cook this,
so don't get all sentimental.

143
00:09:41,809 --> 00:09:44,011
I bought the side dishes.
They're guaranteed to be good.

144
00:09:44,638 --> 00:09:46,256
What's gotten into you?
You're making me uncomfortable.

145
00:09:46,605 --> 00:09:49,262
Is this your way of paying me back
for the seaweed soup?

146
00:09:49,445 --> 00:09:51,304
Why would we need to repay each other?

147
00:09:51,912 --> 00:09:54,961
I'm just grateful, and I feel bad.

148
00:09:55,672 --> 00:09:58,195
I'm grateful for how well you treat Ji Ni,

149
00:09:59,092 --> 00:10:01,783
and I feel bad every time I see your leg.

150
00:10:04,872 --> 00:10:06,830
Prosthetic technology has come a long way.

151
00:10:07,031 --> 00:10:09,736
There'll be even more breakthroughs
in the future.

152
00:10:10,005 --> 00:10:12,066
Are you investing in anything?

153
00:10:12,478 --> 00:10:14,750
With what money?
I only have a little in stocks.

154
00:10:14,832 --> 00:10:15,992
I'll invest more when I earn more.

155
00:10:17,105 --> 00:10:19,615
I heard Grandpa gave my mom some gold.

156
00:10:20,069 --> 00:10:22,376
She won't even let me see it.

157
00:10:22,605 --> 00:10:23,888
I'd like to invest it.

158
00:10:24,567 --> 00:10:25,567
Gold?

159
00:10:25,952 --> 00:10:27,440
I heard about it through the grapevine.

160
00:10:27,945 --> 00:10:31,065
Mom and Seung Hyun won't tell me a thing.
It's so unfair.

161
00:10:31,152 --> 00:10:33,542
I'm too old to still be treated
like the baby of the family.

162
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:38,649
Yeah. I'll do some modeling
and invest when I earn more.

163
00:10:40,518 --> 00:10:41,518
Really?

164
00:10:41,839 --> 00:10:44,595
I told you. I feel responsible.

165
00:10:45,851 --> 00:10:48,396
Thanks for being a big brother to Ji Ni.

166
00:10:48,752 --> 00:10:50,428
I'm older than her, you know.

167
00:10:50,958 --> 00:10:52,730
It's only natural I'd look out for her.

168
00:11:03,831 --> 00:11:04,831
Big Brother.

169
00:11:10,242 --> 00:11:12,824
It was 200,000 dollars.
Why is it suddenly 300,000?

170
00:11:12,872 --> 00:11:14,254
Don't you know what interest is?

171
00:11:15,232 --> 00:11:17,429
You idiot. You don't know anything.

172
00:11:17,605 --> 00:11:18,917
This makes no sense.

173
00:11:19,890 --> 00:11:22,543
How could the interest suddenly go up
by 100,000 dollars in just one week?

174
00:11:24,258 --> 00:11:25,665
Report us if you think it's unfair.

175
00:11:25,838 --> 00:11:28,205
But you're too chicken to report us.

176
00:11:28,412 --> 00:11:33,621
I don't know where you found someone
willing to bankroll you,

177
00:11:34,242 --> 00:11:35,559
but how about sharing some with us?

178
00:11:36,591 --> 00:11:37,858
Eyes down!

179
00:11:38,024 --> 00:11:39,298
I'll gouge your eyes out!

180
00:11:46,332 --> 00:11:47,422
Write it down here.

181
00:11:48,033 --> 00:11:49,752
Write that 100,000 dollars
settles everything.

182
00:11:49,831 --> 00:11:51,161
Otherwise, I can't bring you the money.

183
00:11:57,952 --> 00:12:00,532
For 100,000 dollars, Lee Cheol's...

184
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:03,273
entire debt...

185
00:12:03,883 --> 00:12:05,235
will be settled.

186
00:12:08,072 --> 00:12:11,081
Look at you, learning and improving,

187
00:12:12,629 --> 00:12:15,511
our student Lee Cheol.
Is that good enough?

188
00:12:20,031 --> 00:12:22,591
- Let's go grab a drink.
- Yes, sir.

189
00:12:49,345 --> 00:12:51,372
Please.

190
00:13:05,728 --> 00:13:07,634
(Na Se Ri)

191
00:13:16,265 --> 00:13:17,991
I agree with Ji Ni.

192
00:13:18,825 --> 00:13:21,494
I said there was no way it could be true
because I didn't want to burden her,

193
00:13:21,812 --> 00:13:25,099
but honestly, I can't believe
she didn't see it while driving.

194
00:13:25,838 --> 00:13:28,027
It was clearly caught on Ji Ni's camera.

195
00:13:28,155 --> 00:13:29,155
Pumseonggak.

196
00:13:29,824 --> 00:13:31,514
- Seung Hyun.
- And this time, she even tried...

197
00:13:31,516 --> 00:13:32,625
to hide the woman from the rice cake shop.

198
00:13:32,918 --> 00:13:35,439
We have no proof,
but she's harboring the culprit.

199
00:13:36,645 --> 00:13:38,974
Don't drive a mother and daughter apart
without evidence.

200
00:13:39,158 --> 00:13:40,871
Ji Ni's already been through enough.

201
00:13:41,632 --> 00:13:43,003
That's why I didn't say anything.

202
00:13:43,424 --> 00:13:44,424
Good.

203
00:13:45,265 --> 00:13:46,265
Honestly,

204
00:13:47,130 --> 00:13:48,598
your dad is the one to blame.

205
00:13:48,725 --> 00:13:52,018
As for Se Ri, she couldn't care less
if someone else's child ran into the road.

206
00:13:52,852 --> 00:13:55,906
I also said some terrible things
to Ji Ni back then.

207
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:57,140
Mom.

208
00:13:57,698 --> 00:13:59,179
Let's just catch the culprit.

209
00:13:59,311 --> 00:14:01,929
Don't let baseless suspicions
weigh on your mind.

210
00:14:02,730 --> 00:14:03,730
Okay.

211
00:14:05,285 --> 00:14:09,294
What will you do if we catch the culprit?
The statute of limitations has expired.

212
00:14:09,295 --> 00:14:11,730
What does that matter?
I'll do the same to him.

213
00:14:12,072 --> 00:14:13,805
I asked because I was afraid
you'd say that.

214
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,069
You can't do that.

215
00:14:15,285 --> 00:14:16,922
All I want is an apology.

216
00:14:17,425 --> 00:14:19,172
Don't take revenge with your own hands.

217
00:14:19,225 --> 00:14:20,992
I'm holding back the urge to kill him.

218
00:14:21,025 --> 00:14:22,025
So what happens then?

219
00:14:22,885 --> 00:14:24,802
One of my sons already has
a shattered leg,

220
00:14:25,015 --> 00:14:27,437
and the other becomes a criminal
trying to get revenge?

221
00:14:27,591 --> 00:14:30,178
Are you going to burn down the whole house
just to kill a bug?

222
00:14:30,179 --> 00:14:33,250
And you're chasing him around
just to hear some empty apology?

223
00:14:35,138 --> 00:14:37,754
That man is probably...

224
00:14:38,418 --> 00:14:40,551
in his forties by now, right?

225
00:14:41,512 --> 00:14:44,820
He has a family of his own.
Don't do anything reckless.

226
00:14:45,612 --> 00:14:48,711
Don't get yourself into trouble.
Make sure you meet him with me.

227
00:14:48,992 --> 00:14:50,437
That's what I came to tell you.

228
00:14:52,898 --> 00:14:53,898
You...

229
00:14:55,204 --> 00:14:56,846
need to wait for Mai.

230
00:14:57,558 --> 00:14:59,618
You need to rebuild your family.

231
00:15:01,098 --> 00:15:03,974
You can't let yourself fall apart too.

232
00:15:04,505 --> 00:15:05,995
I couldn't live with that.

233
00:15:07,645 --> 00:15:09,120
I'll contact you once I find him.

234
00:15:09,392 --> 00:15:10,392
We'll talk then.

235
00:15:14,378 --> 00:15:15,579
Mom and Jung A?

236
00:15:16,048 --> 00:15:17,612
Just keep an eye on things.

237
00:15:18,612 --> 00:15:20,688
Ji Ni tends to overlook things like this.

238
00:15:21,105 --> 00:15:22,874
I don't think you should ignore it either.

239
00:15:23,928 --> 00:15:25,294
I don't know.

240
00:15:25,564 --> 00:15:26,934
Something feels off.

241
00:15:28,051 --> 00:15:29,698
You used to call me Sensitive Ji Hu,

242
00:15:29,722 --> 00:15:31,330
but now you're Sensitive Tae O.

243
00:15:32,112 --> 00:15:33,743
Even at Mom's birthday a few days ago,

244
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:36,449
Jung A went all out to entertain them.
She really tried hard.

245
00:15:37,152 --> 00:15:38,449
You're reading way too much into it.

246
00:15:38,558 --> 00:15:40,378
I'd be happy if that were all it was.

247
00:15:40,865 --> 00:15:43,823
But my gut keeps sounding the alarm.

248
00:15:43,848 --> 00:15:45,850
Then ignore it.

249
00:15:46,985 --> 00:15:49,465
Hey, you're the one who needs to wake up.

250
00:15:50,064 --> 00:15:51,753
Jung A likes you.

251
00:15:53,136 --> 00:15:54,136
Right.

252
00:15:54,321 --> 00:15:55,724
She wanted to come here to see you...

253
00:15:55,827 --> 00:15:57,551
but had no excuse, so she came with Mom.

254
00:15:57,750 --> 00:16:00,190
Exactly. You're the one
who's clueless, idiot.

255
00:16:01,263 --> 00:16:02,665
What? She likes me?

256
00:16:02,689 --> 00:16:05,292
Yeah. It's obvious
she's got feelings for someone.

257
00:16:05,317 --> 00:16:06,317
So what?

258
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:07,898
Is she seeing anyone besides you?

259
00:16:07,922 --> 00:16:09,232
No. It's you.

260
00:16:09,469 --> 00:16:10,469
Right?

261
00:16:13,958 --> 00:16:15,822
I honestly don't know what to say.

262
00:16:16,325 --> 00:16:18,795
How did someone this clueless
ever manage to get married?

263
00:16:19,572 --> 00:16:20,960
Man, I feel bad for Ji Ni.

264
00:16:20,985 --> 00:16:22,938
Don't call her Ji Ni, idiot.
Show my wife some respect.

265
00:16:23,039 --> 00:16:24,974
Respect? You're younger than me.

266
00:16:25,092 --> 00:16:26,982
You're No. 2 in Sunshine Class. I'm No. 1.

267
00:16:27,007 --> 00:16:29,171
The one who got married first
outranks you.

268
00:16:29,195 --> 00:16:30,917
Come back when you've tied the knot, kid.

269
00:16:31,174 --> 00:16:32,174
Okay?

270
00:16:33,252 --> 00:16:36,210
Anyway, keep an eye on things.
I'm serious.

271
00:16:36,345 --> 00:16:38,388
Okay.

272
00:16:46,058 --> 00:16:47,058
How do they feel?

273
00:16:47,681 --> 00:16:49,206
They're really comfortable.

274
00:16:49,525 --> 00:16:52,147
My daughter kept recommending them,
so I came to try them on myself.

275
00:16:52,171 --> 00:16:53,604
Good call.

276
00:16:53,865 --> 00:16:55,815
You should always try shoes on first...

277
00:16:55,839 --> 00:16:58,155
and pick a pair that fits just right
and feels comfortable.

278
00:16:58,972 --> 00:17:00,592
- Sun Kyung!
- Sa Bin.

279
00:17:00,617 --> 00:17:03,919
These look nice!

280
00:17:04,616 --> 00:17:05,943
- You're here?
- Yeah.

281
00:17:06,492 --> 00:17:08,558
I'm buying a pair for Yeong Ju.

282
00:17:08,722 --> 00:17:11,373
You know I recommended this brand, right?

283
00:17:11,428 --> 00:17:13,579
Of course. Thank you.

284
00:17:14,118 --> 00:17:15,593
Go ahead and pick something nice.

285
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:16,690
Take your pick, Yeong Ju.

286
00:17:17,096 --> 00:17:18,096
Okay.

287
00:17:20,029 --> 00:17:21,208
These are pretty.

288
00:17:22,852 --> 00:17:24,142
Yeong Ju, I like these.

289
00:17:24,270 --> 00:17:25,423
Try these on.

290
00:17:25,647 --> 00:17:26,647
Okay.

291
00:17:26,735 --> 00:17:29,651
I have no problem paying a fair price
for something good.

292
00:17:30,859 --> 00:17:34,251
I heard you two fought on my birthday
over the gift you bought me.

293
00:17:34,329 --> 00:17:36,425
It's way too expensive for me.

294
00:17:36,705 --> 00:17:38,867
Besides, you already have so many bags.

295
00:17:38,892 --> 00:17:41,118
See? Everyone has their own way
of thinking.

296
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:43,392
Isn't it wasteful to have
so many cheap bags from the market?

297
00:17:43,625 --> 00:17:46,469
What's wrong with having plenty of bags
that suit my lifestyle?

298
00:17:46,862 --> 00:17:48,168
Okay, Sun Kyung.

299
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:50,508
I'll just live within my means.

300
00:17:50,712 --> 00:17:54,037
It's only natural to ask my husband
to spend within our means.

301
00:17:54,298 --> 00:17:56,857
I've told you, Sa Bin.
You need to raise your standards.

302
00:17:58,325 --> 00:18:01,740
Even Yeong Ju's nagging
sounds like music to my ears.

303
00:18:02,472 --> 00:18:06,332
Yeong Ju, your feet need to be comfortable
if you're going to wear them all day.

304
00:18:06,372 --> 00:18:08,713
Let's wear these and keep walking together
for many years to come.

305
00:18:14,771 --> 00:18:15,771
Ma'am.

306
00:18:16,918 --> 00:18:18,484
Hello.

307
00:18:18,812 --> 00:18:20,120
Are you here to buy shoes?

308
00:18:20,122 --> 00:18:22,494
Yeah, what brings you here?

309
00:18:22,542 --> 00:18:24,924
I love these shoes too.
They're so comfortable.

310
00:18:26,165 --> 00:18:29,264
I wear them every day.
Today I'm buying a pair as a gift.

311
00:18:30,226 --> 00:18:31,744
Jung A, you're here.

312
00:18:31,769 --> 00:18:33,597
- Hello.
- Good to see you.

313
00:18:33,621 --> 00:18:34,621
Have you eaten?

314
00:18:34,645 --> 00:18:35,963
Not yet.

315
00:18:36,305 --> 00:18:39,574
Ma'am, I'm starving.

316
00:18:40,501 --> 00:18:42,308
Could you treat me to a meal?

317
00:18:43,107 --> 00:18:45,628
I've been talking all day
and taking care of academy business.

318
00:18:45,946 --> 00:18:47,488
Poor thing. Okay.

319
00:18:47,513 --> 00:18:48,777
Do you like omakase?

320
00:18:49,058 --> 00:18:50,277
Omakase?

321
00:18:51,098 --> 00:18:53,451
My mouth's already watering.

322
00:18:54,447 --> 00:18:56,104
You're such a cutie.

323
00:18:56,332 --> 00:18:59,805
Any family would be lucky
to have a daughter-in-law like you.

324
00:19:00,445 --> 00:19:01,672
There you go again.

325
00:19:01,851 --> 00:19:02,851
Please don't, ma'am.

326
00:19:03,209 --> 00:19:04,515
People will get the wrong idea.

327
00:19:05,511 --> 00:19:06,921
You little sweetheart.

328
00:19:08,385 --> 00:19:09,643
Anything else you'd like to eat?

329
00:19:10,103 --> 00:19:12,401
- Omakase sounds wonderful already.
- Have it all.

330
00:19:12,448 --> 00:19:14,456
- I'll eat anything.
- Want me to get you some ice cream?

331
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,480
Okay.

332
00:19:21,864 --> 00:19:22,864
What?

333
00:19:29,371 --> 00:19:30,440
You startled me.

334
00:19:31,141 --> 00:19:32,141
When did you get here?

335
00:19:32,644 --> 00:19:33,644
Your hair...

336
00:19:33,805 --> 00:19:36,598
The weather's getting chilly,
so I felt like cutting it.

337
00:19:36,966 --> 00:19:39,375
Don't people usually grow it out
when it gets cold?

338
00:19:39,659 --> 00:19:41,719
Stylish people do the opposite.

339
00:19:43,458 --> 00:19:45,093
Are you sure there's nothing behind it?

340
00:19:45,958 --> 00:19:49,088
I just want to focus on work,
like I'm heading into the army.

341
00:19:49,911 --> 00:19:52,161
I'm sick of Mom and Seung Hyun
keeping tabs on me.

342
00:19:52,658 --> 00:19:53,962
I feel like I need to prove myself.

343
00:19:54,528 --> 00:19:55,610
Anyway, it suits you.

344
00:19:55,757 --> 00:19:56,843
It's the handsome face.

345
00:19:57,325 --> 00:19:58,580
Did you bring your drawings?

346
00:19:59,154 --> 00:20:00,480
Yes.

347
00:20:00,672 --> 00:20:02,859
They're just sketches for now.

348
00:20:04,832 --> 00:20:07,096
Let your big brother take a look.

349
00:20:09,985 --> 00:20:11,410
Your mom...

350
00:20:11,473 --> 00:20:13,634
told me to be a better brother to you.

351
00:20:14,511 --> 00:20:15,511
Have I been that bad?

352
00:20:16,208 --> 00:20:18,250
No, you've been good to me.

353
00:20:18,274 --> 00:20:19,274
Of course I have.

354
00:20:19,591 --> 00:20:22,403
Things were so different
around this time last year.

355
00:20:25,192 --> 00:20:26,192
Hey.

356
00:20:26,749 --> 00:20:28,359
Two hundred...

357
00:20:29,565 --> 00:20:30,811
Didn't your hand cramp up?

358
00:20:31,245 --> 00:20:33,673
You're a newlywed.
Have you done nothing but draw?

359
00:20:36,838 --> 00:20:40,051
You're a real workaholic, aren't you?

360
00:20:40,867 --> 00:20:41,867
A bit.

361
00:20:41,892 --> 00:20:44,307
Seung Hyun and I go all in
when we get into something too.

362
00:20:44,390 --> 00:20:45,893
Mom's always scolding us for it.

363
00:20:47,203 --> 00:20:48,203
Maybe we're alike.

364
00:20:51,732 --> 00:20:53,564
Great. I'll try working with these.

365
00:20:53,789 --> 00:20:55,262
Okay. Thank you.

366
00:20:56,311 --> 00:20:57,930
I can't pay you much...

367
00:21:01,838 --> 00:21:02,838
But at least take this.

368
00:21:09,177 --> 00:21:10,810
(Deposit 500 dollars, Cha Seung Woo)

369
00:21:11,076 --> 00:21:12,809
You don't have to pay me.

370
00:21:13,845 --> 00:21:17,846
I agreed to draw your mom's portrait.

371
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:21,036
I'm going to the studio.
I'll treat her to something nice.

372
00:21:21,713 --> 00:21:22,713
Drawing again?

373
00:21:31,551 --> 00:21:33,218
Jung A's at the shop?

374
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:39,489
When I offered to go,
Mother told me not to come.

375
00:21:40,484 --> 00:21:42,217
She said I'd embarrass her.

376
00:21:42,287 --> 00:21:43,287
What?

377
00:21:43,998 --> 00:21:46,049
That's going too far.

378
00:21:46,631 --> 00:21:48,982
She never knows when to hold her tongue.

379
00:21:50,752 --> 00:21:52,603
I guess she hates me that much.

380
00:21:53,325 --> 00:21:54,922
Don't be discouraged. Do your best.

381
00:21:55,310 --> 00:21:59,550
Ask Jung A to stay away for now.

382
00:21:59,575 --> 00:22:01,340
How can I ask her that?

383
00:22:01,365 --> 00:22:02,733
Why couldn't you?

384
00:22:03,291 --> 00:22:05,899
She doesn't feel close to you yet.
Things are still awkward.

385
00:22:05,924 --> 00:22:07,360
Tell Jung A to see her later.

386
00:22:18,225 --> 00:22:20,354
I got you a gift.

387
00:22:20,924 --> 00:22:21,924
Thank you.

388
00:22:22,765 --> 00:22:24,593
I heard you stopped by Mother's shop.

389
00:22:24,618 --> 00:22:28,358
Yes. I was really hungry after class,

390
00:22:28,382 --> 00:22:30,105
so she took me out for omakase.

391
00:22:30,130 --> 00:22:33,759
It was delicious.
The meat melted in my mouth...

392
00:22:33,783 --> 00:22:34,783
Jung A.

393
00:22:36,878 --> 00:22:37,878
Could you...

394
00:22:39,322 --> 00:22:42,741
take things a little slower
with my mother-in-law?

395
00:22:42,911 --> 00:22:43,911
Why?

396
00:22:44,592 --> 00:22:46,018
What do you mean?

397
00:22:46,078 --> 00:22:48,152
You know I get along with older people.

398
00:22:48,283 --> 00:22:49,352
Even your mom...

399
00:22:49,353 --> 00:22:51,663
I know. You make friends easily.

400
00:22:52,506 --> 00:22:55,355
But she's my mother-in-law.

401
00:22:55,987 --> 00:22:58,257
You can be close,
but I'm still her daughter-in-law.

402
00:23:00,665 --> 00:23:03,430
I still find it hard to be around her,

403
00:23:04,227 --> 00:23:06,752
and I don't have a place in her heart yet.

404
00:23:08,732 --> 00:23:11,340
This isn't easy for me to say,

405
00:23:11,843 --> 00:23:13,472
but could you slow down a little...

406
00:23:13,942 --> 00:23:17,455
until I've gotten closer to her?

407
00:23:18,906 --> 00:23:20,050
Ji Ni.

408
00:23:21,616 --> 00:23:23,463
I'm sorry. Please do this for me.

409
00:23:25,185 --> 00:23:26,233
Am I the one being unreasonable?

410
00:23:26,631 --> 00:23:28,161
I wouldn't say that.

411
00:23:28,965 --> 00:23:31,169
I really didn't mean anything by it,

412
00:23:32,393 --> 00:23:35,599
but hearing you say that
puts me in an awkward position.

413
00:23:37,285 --> 00:23:38,635
In the past,

414
00:23:39,472 --> 00:23:42,132
I gave up on everything
and avoided it all.

415
00:23:43,285 --> 00:23:45,021
But I can't do that now.

416
00:23:45,365 --> 00:23:48,451
I need to get closer to her
so Ji Hu can feel at ease too.

417
00:23:50,254 --> 00:23:52,254
I can't keep looking the other way.

418
00:23:53,024 --> 00:23:54,405
That's right.

419
00:23:54,844 --> 00:23:57,148
I'm going to try. Please help me.

420
00:23:58,072 --> 00:23:59,261
Are you upset?

421
00:24:00,951 --> 00:24:02,882
I'm a little taken aback.

422
00:24:04,425 --> 00:24:06,703
How many times have I even seen her?

423
00:24:06,898 --> 00:24:10,727
I just bought shoes I liked
and made a quick birthday visit.

424
00:24:10,752 --> 00:24:12,543
I can see why you'd feel that way.

425
00:24:13,025 --> 00:24:15,016
I've never said this to you before.

426
00:24:15,478 --> 00:24:16,478
But...

427
00:24:17,524 --> 00:24:20,137
I'm Ji Hu's wife.
I'm her daughter-in-law now.

428
00:24:21,852 --> 00:24:25,062
But even in front of me...

429
00:24:26,377 --> 00:24:29,530
she says she wishes
she had a daughter-in-law like you.

430
00:24:29,894 --> 00:24:32,339
- You heard her too.
- No, that's...

431
00:24:34,453 --> 00:24:36,287
I told her myself...

432
00:24:36,312 --> 00:24:37,997
not to say things like that!

433
00:24:43,771 --> 00:24:45,639
I know you mean well.

434
00:24:47,032 --> 00:24:51,204
You get along with everyone so easily.

435
00:24:51,792 --> 00:24:53,370
But I don't.

436
00:24:53,565 --> 00:24:55,182
I'm having a really hard time.

437
00:24:57,745 --> 00:25:01,525
So please give me some time, for my sake.

438
00:25:02,318 --> 00:25:03,591
That's all I'm asking.

439
00:25:04,386 --> 00:25:05,386
Okay?

440
00:25:07,258 --> 00:25:08,498
Okay.

441
00:25:16,803 --> 00:25:20,533
Perfect. Let's do one more.

442
00:25:22,036 --> 00:25:23,694
Very good.

443
00:25:24,952 --> 00:25:26,965
Let's try one more.

444
00:25:27,245 --> 00:25:30,046
I never thought I'd end up
being Na Se Ri's bodyguard.

445
00:25:38,365 --> 00:25:39,983
Yes, that's good.

446
00:25:40,906 --> 00:25:43,639
Just a little smile.
That's it. A warm, motherly smile.

447
00:25:43,664 --> 00:25:44,753
Let the logo show a little.

448
00:25:45,636 --> 00:25:47,163
Very good.

449
00:25:47,652 --> 00:25:49,050
One more, please.

450
00:25:50,758 --> 00:25:52,130
That's all for today.

451
00:25:52,155 --> 00:25:53,950
Well done. Thank you.

452
00:25:53,974 --> 00:25:56,716
- Thanks for your work.
- Thank you too.

453
00:26:11,671 --> 00:26:12,704
Ma'am.

454
00:26:15,271 --> 00:26:18,103
How did you get here...

455
00:26:28,245 --> 00:26:29,752
I told you to stay away, didn't I?

456
00:26:29,899 --> 00:26:31,342
We agreed never to see each other again.

457
00:26:31,511 --> 00:26:33,731
I told you if you showed up again,
we'd both be dead, didn't I?

458
00:26:33,979 --> 00:26:35,138
You think I'm joking?

459
00:26:35,804 --> 00:26:37,198
Yes, I do.

460
00:26:37,645 --> 00:26:41,067
So many people have threatened to kill me.
You don't really scare me.

461
00:26:41,878 --> 00:26:44,308
Give me another 100,000 dollars.

462
00:26:44,432 --> 00:26:45,934
I'll really say goodbye for good.

463
00:26:45,958 --> 00:26:47,160
What?

464
00:26:47,723 --> 00:26:49,460
You scumbag.

465
00:26:50,178 --> 00:26:51,806
This looks nice.

466
00:26:51,830 --> 00:26:53,772
Don't touch that! Let go!

467
00:26:54,841 --> 00:26:55,841
Come on!

468
00:26:57,260 --> 00:26:58,887
Se Ri!

469
00:26:58,912 --> 00:27:01,095
- Where are you?
- I'm here!

470
00:27:03,144 --> 00:27:04,144
Get lost.

471
00:27:05,095 --> 00:27:06,146
A hundred thousand dollars.

472
00:27:06,405 --> 00:27:07,493
Have it ready fast.

473
00:27:17,425 --> 00:27:19,395
What are you doing here? What's wrong?

474
00:27:19,420 --> 00:27:21,529
I have a headache...

475
00:27:38,989 --> 00:27:40,095
Hey.

476
00:27:41,102 --> 00:27:42,853
I warned you I'd be keeping an eye on you.

477
00:27:43,159 --> 00:27:45,766
You took the money.
You should've stayed away, you punk.

478
00:27:47,569 --> 00:27:49,896
I had a feeling you'd be around.

479
00:27:57,132 --> 00:28:00,068
Na Se Ri and I are splitting
the money for that leg.

480
00:28:00,093 --> 00:28:03,511
Interfere again, and I'll kill you.
You'd better watch yourself, you punk.

481
00:28:06,594 --> 00:28:08,527
Money for that leg?

482
00:28:08,597 --> 00:28:09,597
Hey!

483
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:13,482
Hey!

484
00:28:52,033 --> 00:28:55,328
(Family Register)

485
00:28:55,398 --> 00:28:57,262
He said you split the money for that leg.

486
00:28:57,287 --> 00:28:59,255
- Have you seen this man before?
- I think I saw him at Ji Ni's wedding.

487
00:28:59,280 --> 00:29:01,672
If we both ruined his leg,
we're accomplices.

488
00:29:01,697 --> 00:29:02,832
Tae O said something strange.

489
00:29:02,857 --> 00:29:04,671
He finds it strange
that Jung A and my mom are so close.

490
00:29:04,696 --> 00:29:06,464
You don't still like Ji Hu, do you?

491
00:29:06,489 --> 00:29:08,510
What about you?
Don't you still like Ji Ni?

492
00:29:08,535 --> 00:29:10,653
You rude little brat.
What you do behind my back...

493
00:29:10,678 --> 00:29:12,131
You're no different from your mom.

494
00:29:12,156 --> 00:29:14,522
Please, can't you be like other moms
just this once?

495
00:29:15,035 --> 00:29:17,035
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
